    "text": "In a Screw Gauge, fifth division of the circular scale coincides with the reference line when the ratchet is closed. There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>&nbsp;divisions on the circular scale, and the main scale moves by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> on a complete rotation. For a particular observation the reading on the main scale is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> and the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>20</mn><mtext>th&#160;</mtext></msup></math> division of the circular scale coincides with reference line. Calculate the true reading.",
